Package: raiden-apps
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @DISTRO_NAME@ <noreply@example.invalid>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, ca-certificates, util-linux, adduser, desktop-file-utils
Recommends: google-chrome-stable, papirus-icon-theme
Description: Third-party apps for @DISTRO_NAME@
 Installs the apps whose makers publish Linux versions only as downloads,
 with launchers, and keeps them current: a timer installs new releases
 while the apps are closed.
  - Google Antigravity, the agent app, and the Antigravity IDE
  - ProtonPlus, which installs Proton-GE and other compatibility tools for
    Steam, Lutris and Heroic
  - Heroic Games Launcher (the image ships its .deb; updates come from here)
 Apps the ISO leaves out (the public edition has no Google Chrome, Claude or
 Antigravity, whose licences do not allow passing them on) are installed
 from their makers the first time the computer is online.
 Also adds Outlook and Microsoft 365 as web apps in their own windows, and
 lets administrators run virtual machines (kvm group), which Claude's
 Cowork tasks use.
